menu "Traffic Light Configuration"

    config TRAFFIC_ENABLE_WIFI
        bool "Enable WiFi + HTTP server + on-screen WiFi setup"
        default y
        help
          Disable for QEMU-only validation builds: QEMU's esp32 machine
          has no WiFi baseband model, so esp_wifi aborts. In that mode a
          fake AP list is used so the on-screen setup UI can still be
          exercised, and the keys drive the traffic light state directly.
          QEMU serial keys: u d l r a b (uppercase = long press),
          p = dump the framebuffer as ASCII art.

    config TRAFFIC_ENABLE_BLE
        bool "Enable the Bluetooth (BLE) link as an alternative to WiFi"
        depends on TRAFFIC_ENABLE_WIFI
        default y
        help
          NimBLE GATT peripheral exposing the same command set as the HTTP
          API (rojo / alerta / verde / off / status / task / decision), so
          the host hook can talk to the console over Bluetooth instead of
          WiFi. Which of the two is active is chosen on the console itself
          (settings menu → 连接) and remembered in NVS.

          Depends on TRAFFIC_ENABLE_WIFI purely because that switch already
          means "real hardware": QEMU's esp32 machine has no Bluetooth
          controller model either, so this is off in QEMU builds.

          Needs CONFIG_BT_ENABLED and CONFIG_BT_NIMBLE_ENABLED (both set in
          sdkconfig.defaults).

endmenu
